demonstrate the SQL comparison operators

13
00:00:40.313 --> 00:00:44.261
in a database, describe the purpose
of an ORDER BY clause, and

14
00:00:44.261 --> 00:00:49.208
demonstrate ascending and descending
sorts by single and multiple columns.

15
00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:53.532
In the videos and filtering the WHERE
clause was used with the SQL select

16
00:00:53.532 --> 00:00:55.415
statement to filter records.

17
00:00:55.415 --> 00:00:59.111
For the WHERE clause, you should
now be able to explain the purpose

18
00:00:59.111 --> 00:01:02.873
